{
  "id": "u2",
  "title": "Unit 2",
  "subtitle": "The beginning of ministry",
  "guide": {
    "summary": "Jesus' ministry begins with his baptism and the confirmation of the Father. He overcomes the temptations in the wilderness and calls his first disciples. His first miracle in Cana reveals his power. Nicodemus learns about being born again. Everything converges on the central truth: God loves the world and offers eternal life through the Son.",
    "keyVerses": [
      {
        "reference": "Matthew 3:16-17",
        "text": "Jesus, when he was baptized, went up directly from the water; and behold, the heavens were opened to him. He saw the Spirit of God descending as a dove, coming on him. And behold, a voice out of the heavens said, \"This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.\""
      },
      {
        "reference": "John 3:16",
        "text": "For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life."
      },
      {
        "reference": "John 1:1",
        "text": "In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God."
      }
    ]
  },
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "u2-l1",
      "title": "John the Baptist and Baptism",
      "icon": "drop.fill",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "u2-l1-e1",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "Complete the verse",
          "text": "\"I indeed baptize you with water for repentance, but he who comes after me is mightier than I, whose shoes I am not worthy to carry. He will baptize you with the ___ and with fire.\"",
          "speaker": "John the Baptist",
          "options": [
            "Holy Spirit",
            "spirit",
            "power",
            "fire"
          ],
          "answer": "Holy Spirit",
          "reference": "Matthew 3:11"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l1-e2",
          "kind": "trueFalse",
          "prompt": "True or false?",
          "statement": "John the Baptist was the Messiah.",
          "isTrue": false,
          "reference": "John 1:20",
          "explanation": "John explicitly denied that he was the Christ (John 1:20), saying he was merely a voice preparing the way."
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l1-e3",
          "kind": "buildVerse",
          "prompt": "Build the verse",
          "text": "John's preparation for Jesus",
          "tokens": [
            "Prepare the way",
            "of the Lord",
            "make straight",
            "his paths"
          ],
          "distractors": [
            "cleanse",
            "of the king",
            "lift up",
            "the roads"
          ],
          "reference": "Matthew 3:3"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l1-e4",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "Where was Jesus baptized?",
          "text": "Jesus was baptized in the river ___.",
          "options": [
            "Jordan",
            "Nile",
            "Euphrates",
            "Tigris"
          ],
          "answer": "Jordan",
          "reference": "Matthew 3:13"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l1-e5",
          "kind": "matchPairs",
          "prompt": "Match the pairs",
          "pairs": [
            {
              "left": "John the Baptist",
              "right": "Prepares the way"
            },
            {
              "left": "Jesus",
              "right": "Fulfills righteousness"
            },
            {
              "left": "Holy Spirit",
              "right": "Descends in form"
            },
            {
              "left": "Voice of God",
              "right": "Approves the Son"
            }
          ],
          "reference": "Matthew 3"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l1-e6",
          "kind": "trueFalse",
          "prompt": "True or false?",
          "statement": "At Jesus' baptism, a voice from heaven confirmed that he was the Son of God.",
          "isTrue": true,
          "reference": "Matthew 3:17",
          "explanation": "A voice from heaven said: \"This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased\" (Matthew 3:17)."
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l1-e7",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "In what form did the Holy Spirit descend on Jesus?",
          "text": "The Holy Spirit descended on Jesus in the form of a ___.",
          "options": [
            "dove",
            "light",
            "fire",
            "wind"
          ],
          "answer": "dove",
          "reference": "Matthew 3:16"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l1-e8",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "Who baptized in the Jordan river?",
          "text": "___ baptized people for repentance of their sins.",
          "speaker": "Narrator",
          "options": [
            "John",
            "Peter",
            "Andrew",
            "Philip"
          ],
          "answer": "John",
          "reference": "Matthew 3:6"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u2-l2",
      "title": "The Temptation in the Wilderness",
      "icon": "flame.fill",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "u2-l2-e1",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "Complete the verse",
          "text": "\"Then Jesus was led up by the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted by the ___. When he had fasted forty days and forty nights, he was hungry.\"",
          "options": [
            "devil",
            "people",
            "high priest",
            "king"
          ],
          "answer": "devil",
          "reference": "Matthew 4:1-2"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l2-e2",
          "kind": "trueFalse",
          "prompt": "True or false?",
          "statement": "Jesus went to the wilderness because he wanted to hide from his enemies.",
          "isTrue": false,
          "reference": "Matthew 4:1",
          "explanation": "Jesus was led by the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted by the devil, not to hide."
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l2-e3",
          "kind": "buildVerse",
          "prompt": "Build the verse",
          "text": "Jesus' response to the first temptation",
          "tokens": [
            "Man shall not live",
            "by bread alone",
            "but by every",
            "word that proceeds",
            "from the mouth of God"
          ],
          "distractors": [
            "by works",
            "of the Spirit",
            "by faith",
            "by his grace"
          ],
          "reference": "Matthew 4:4"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l2-e4",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "What was the first temptation offered to Jesus?",
          "text": "The devil asked Jesus to turn the ___ into bread.",
          "options": [
            "stones",
            "sand",
            "rocks",
            "ground"
          ],
          "answer": "stones",
          "reference": "Matthew 4:3"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l2-e5",
          "kind": "matchPairs",
          "prompt": "Match the pairs",
          "pairs": [
            {
              "left": "First temptation",
              "right": "Bread of wilderness"
            },
            {
              "left": "Second temptation",
              "right": "Power of kingdoms"
            },
            {
              "left": "Third temptation",
              "right": "Throw from temple"
            },
            {
              "left": "Scripture",
              "right": "Weapon against devil"
            }
          ],
          "reference": "Matthew 4:1-11"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l2-e6",
          "kind": "trueFalse",
          "prompt": "True or false?",
          "statement": "The devil offered Jesus all the kingdoms of the world if he would worship him.",
          "isTrue": true,
          "reference": "Matthew 4:8-9",
          "explanation": "The devil took Jesus to a high mountain and showed him all the kingdoms, offering them for worship (Matthew 4:8-9)."
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l2-e7",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "How did Jesus always respond to the temptations?",
          "text": "Jesus responded with verses from the ___.",
          "options": [
            "Scripture",
            "tradition",
            "wisdom",
            "oral law"
          ],
          "answer": "Scripture",
          "reference": "Matthew 4:4,7,10"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2-l2-e8",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "How many days did Jesus fast in the wilderness?",
          "text": "Jesus fasted for ___ days and ___ nights.",
          "options": [
            "forty and forty",
            "thirty and thirty",
            "twenty and twenty",
            "ten and ten"
          ],
          "answer": "forty and forty",
          "reference": "Matthew 4:2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
